{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno5_eno1_signed_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc",
    "description": "Hybrid WENO5/ENO1 gradient magnitude |grad u| = sqrt(u_x^2 + u_y^2) for the level-set REINITIALISATION equation psi_tau = S(psi_0)(1 - |grad psi|) of NCAR fire_behavior (physics/level_set_mod.F90 Advance_ls_reinit, fire_upwinding_reinit = 4; Sussman, Smereka & Osher 1994 as adapted by Munoz-Esparza et al. 2018), on cartesian_uniform_2d with the linear-extrapolation halo closure. It differs from rules/weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc only in its interior stencils, stencils/weno5_eno1_signed_D1x_interior and stencils/weno5_eno1_signed_D1y_interior: the upwind side is chosen by the frozen sign field instead of the wind, and the band test that selects WENO5 over ENO1 is SIGNED rather than absolute, as the reference writes it (see the stencils, including why the missing abs() is reproduced rather than corrected). The sign field is the free name `upwind_sign` ([x, y]; fire_behavior's lfn_s0, S(psi_0) = psi_0 / sqrt(psi_0^2 + dx^2) frozen at the start of the pseudo-time iteration), bound to the stencils' param s; the rule references no wind_u/wind_v. COMPOUND MATCH (esm-spec 9.6.3): the whole compound sqrt((D(u, wrt: x))^2 + (D(u, wrt: y))^2) at priority 20, scoped with where {u: {shape: [x, y]}} -- the same pattern and priority as rules/weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc, because it is another discretization of the same operator |grad u|. Which one lowers a component's norm is chosen by which rule that component imports (esm-spec 9.6.8: choosing a scheme = choosing a rule); a component imports one of them. Importing two is deterministic but pointless: the 9.6.3 declaration-order tie-break gives every match to the first declared, and the other never fires. Propagation and reinitialisation are separate components (a tendency model and a pseudo-time model), each importing its own. The body is sqrt(Mx^2 + My^2) with Mx, My the family's per-axis frames (rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame, rules/weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_frame: the ENO1 strips and one-cell guarded linear-extrapolation ghosts of fire_behavior's Extrapol_var_at_bdys, lint-tiled in their own files) around this rule's own interior stencils. ORDER: tagged order:1 for the same reason as its sibling -- the ENO1 branch and the wall closure are first-order, and the fifth-order branch applies only inside the band, so no whole-field convergence claim is made and no convergence case is shipped. Free names: upwind_sign, bdy_eno1_cells, weno_band_cells, dx, dy. Requires NX, NY >= 7.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:grad_norm",
      "axes:x,y",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:7",
      "bc:extrapolate_linear",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Sussman, M., Smereka, P., & Osher, S. (1994). A level set approach for computing solutions to incompressible two-phase flow. Journal of Computational Physics, 114(1), 146-159. The reinitialisation equation psi_tau = S(psi_0)(1 - |grad psi|) with the smoothed sign S(psi_0) = psi_0/sqrt(psi_0^2 + dx^2).",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1994.1155"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P. A., & Coen, J. L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 10(4), 908-926. The hybrid WENO5/ENO1 level-set scheme (fire_upwinding = 9) of WRF-Fire / NCAR fire_behavior.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical WENO5 smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Harten, A., Engquist, B., Osher, S., & Chakravarthy, S. R. (1987). Uniformly high order accurate essentially non-oscillatory schemes, III. Journal of Computational Physics, 71(2), 231-303. ENO stencil selection by smallest divided difference (first-order form: the minmod limiter).",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(87)90031-3"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Advance_ls_reinit (fire_upwinding_reinit = 4), Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_frame.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/weno5_eno1_signed_D1x_interior.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/weno5_eno1_signed_D1y_interior.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno5_eno1_signed_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc": {
      "params": [
        "u"
      ],
      "priority": 20,
      "match": {
        "op": "sqrt",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "x"
                  },
                  2
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "y"
                  },
                  2
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "where": {
        "u": {
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "sqrt",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame",
                    "bindings": {
                      "u": "u",
                      "interior": {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "weno5_eno1_signed_D1x_interior",
                        "bindings": {
                          "u": "u",
                          "s": "upwind_sign"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  2
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_frame",
                    "bindings": {
                      "u": "u",
                      "interior": {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "weno5_eno1_signed_D1y_interior",
                        "bindings": {
                          "u": "u",
                          "s": "upwind_sign"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  2
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
